</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Hi, DcMan.<br>
<br>
A cieling fan motor may be what you're looking for.  This is a rim drive motor and is differently wound than most motors.  The coils remain stationary, projecting their field outwards, while the rim - without coils - rotates.  If you power the motor - without the rim - through a commutator, its field will rotate.  This rotation can be enhanced by an additional, normal motor, using a belt and pulleys which spin the fan motor's shaft.  (The shaft normally doesn't turn.)  A suitable commutator is available as part of an extention cord reel which plugs in and provides power as the cord is pulled out from the reel.  Or do you need a rotating vertical field? -JV<br><br></td></tr>
